# Frozen Interfaces

Everything under `common/`, `Simulator/common_simulator/`, and
`MissionControl/common_mission_control/` is published by the course and used **as-is** (e18). Do not
change a signature, add a member, add a file, or move a header between these folders.

**Before committing anything that touches these folders, or before submission, verify compliance —
don't eyeball it:**

- Quick check (git-based, tracks `main`): `.cursor/skills/verify-frozen-interfaces/SKILL.md`.
- Deep audit (subagent-based, diffs against the actual pristine `ex_3_skeleton` checkout, not just
  `main`): `.cursor/skills/verify-interfaces-vs-skeleton/SKILL.md`.

Full delta table: `docs/api-delta-ex2-to-ex3.md`. The parts that break ported ex2 code:

## Include paths and namespaces

| Ex2 | Ex3 |
|-----|-----|
| `<drone_mapper/IMap3D.h>`, namespace `drone_mapper` | `<Common/IMap3D.h>`, namespace `common` |
| `<drone_mapper/ISimulation.h>` | `<Simulator/ISimulation.h>`, namespace `simulator` |
| `<drone_mapper/IDroneControl.h>` | `<MissionControl/IDroneControl.h>`, namespace `mission_control` |
| `types::` (one namespace) | `common::types::` and `simulator::types::` |

`Common/Types.h` no longer includes the simulation types — `SimulationTypes.h` is Simulator-private, so
plugins cannot see `SimulationCompositionData` or `SimulationManagerReport`.

## Dependency structs replace constructor arguments

`IMappingAlgorithm` takes `MappingAlgorithmDependencies`; mission-control plugins are constructed from
`MissionControlDependencies` (`Common/MissionControlFactory.h`). Both are passed **by value** by the
registration macros, so concrete classes need `explicit Impl(Dependencies)`.

`MissionControlDependencies` carries `output_map_file` and `verbose`, and its `drone_config` comment says
"mission will create its own drone controller" — so `DroneControl` is constructed **inside**
`MissionControlImpl`, not by the simulator.

## Removed / renamed fields

- `config_load_error` is gone from `DroneConfigData`, `LidarConfigData`, `MissionConfigData`, and
  `SimulationConfigData`. Carry parse errors in our own `UserCommon` result type instead.
- `MissionConfigData::boundaries` → `MissionConfigData::mission_bounds`.
- `MappingStepCommand::fusion_max` is gone — always fuse at full lidar `z_max`.
- `VoxelOccupancy` is now `: signed char`; `Position3D` has `operator+` / `operator-`.

## Composition shape

`SimulationCompositionData` now holds
`std::vector<std::tuple<SimulationConfigData, std::vector<MissionConfigData>>> simulation_mission_groups`
plus `drone_configs` / `lidar_configs`. The set of runs is unchanged: **(simulation, mission) pairs ×
drone_configs × lidar_configs**.

## Semantics unchanged from ex2

- `nextStep(state, latest_scan)` — `latest_scan` may be `nullptr` on the first call.
- Algorithms read the output map through `const IMap3D&` and **never** write voxels; the drone controller
  writes scan results.
- `IMap3D` exposes `atVoxel`, `getMapConfig`, `isInBounds`; `IMutableMap3D` adds `set` and `save`.
- `MapConfig` bundles boundaries + offset + resolution.
- Drone-control step order: read GPS state → `algorithm.nextStep(...)` → movement (validated) → scan →
  convert to voxels → `output_map.set(...)` → return `DroneStepResult`.

## Not provided anymore

Ex2 shipped `MockLidar` and `ScanResultToVoxels`; ex3 ships **neither**, nor `Map3DImpl`, `MockGPS`,
`MockMovement`, or `MapsComparison`. All of it is ours to port — see `docs/component-placement.md`.
